# Repository laws (identical for every agent)

Canonical instructions: `AGENTS.md`. Prefer it over tool-specific defaults on
process conflicts. Architecture goal law lives in
`.cursor/rules/decode-invariants.mdc` and `docs/design/decode-invariants.md`.

Parity across harnesses is enforced by
`python -m scripts.verify_agent_surfaces`; the gaps this rule closes are
recorded in `docs/design/agent-harness-parity-audit.md`.

Skills are canonical under `.agents/skills/`; `.cursor/skills/` holds discovery
symlinks. Edit only the canonical copy.

- **Hard run cap.** Every train / eval / bench / profile / matrix run and its
  supporting shell commands obey `MAX_RUN_MINUTES` in
  `src/slm_training/levers.py`. A timed out, interrupted, or killed run is
  never evidence.
- **Iron law: docs follow every experiment.** After any train / eval /
  benchmark / profile / telemetry / matrix / reproduction run, use the
  `documenting-experiment-results` skill. Numbers only in `outputs/`, chat, or
  a PR comment are incomplete work.
- **Honest ship gates.** Use `honest-ship-eval` when evaluating, writing or
  interpreting ship gates, changing parse/fidelity/reward metrics, or claiming
  readiness. Say fixture-demo vs ship; never weaken a gate to green CI.
- **Data-quality law.** After any training-data build or synthesis, use
  `synthesis-feedback` — read the build's `quality_report.json`,
  `rejected.jsonl`, and `synthesis_feedback.json`, and improve the synthesis
  harness from that evidence. Never weaken the gates.
- **Model card.** When a checkpoint is created, synced, bootstrapped, or
  promoted, update `docs/MODEL_CARD.md` **and** the README model-card summary.
- **Version stamps.** Results carry `version_stamp`; changing a watched
  metric / gate / harness / matrix / data-builder file requires a component
  bump (or a `no-bump:` history note) in
  `src/slm_training/resources/versions.json` —
  `python -m scripts.verify_version_stamps --check` enforces it.
- **External test cases.** Agents edit mirrored JSON cases under
  `src/slm_training/resources/test_cases/` and refresh snapshots with
  `python -m scripts.refresh_test_cases <test-or-resource>`. Ordinary tests and
  CI stay read-only; run `refresh_test_cases --check --changed` before finishing.
- **Dashboard parity.** When you change a dashboard page
  (`src/apps/dashboard/src/pages/*.tsx`), keep its interpreted-mode
  `src/slm_training/web/static/openui/*.openui` program at parity and run
  `python scripts/validate_page_dsl.py` — use the `dashboard-openui-parity`
  skill.
- **Preregistered campaigns.** AP-007+ experiment runners and every promotion
  candidate use the `ExperimentCampaignV1` contract in
  `src/slm_training/autoresearch/experiment_campaign.py`. Never replace the
  locked confirmatory endpoint, arms, seeds, stopping rule, family, or gates
  after outcomes are visible.
- **Repository organization.** Use `organize-repository` before creating,
  moving, renaming, deleting, or duplicating tracked paths, and use `git mv`
  for every tracked relocation.

Cursor has no committed hook configuration in this repo, so the raw-`mv` guard
and post-edit dashboard/version checks that Claude Code and Codex get do not
run for you. Run them yourself before finishing:

```bash
python -m scripts.repo_policy
.githooks/check-changed
```
